 a metadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4156031\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: wsvn.com\nSLUG: george-santos-reported-to-prosecutors-over-suspicious-kalshi-trades-ap-source-says\nTEXT: George Santos, a former Republican congressman, has been reported to prosecutors over suspicious Kalshi trades. Santos, who won office after inventing a bogus persona as a Wall Street dealmaker, was sentenced to seven years in prison for fraud and identity theft in 2024. Prediction markets, including Kalshi and Polymarket, have faced scrutiny over their business practices, with some lawmakers urging them to do more to prevent insider trading. In April, a soldier was charged with using classified information to win over $400,000 predicting the capture of Venezuelan President Nicolás Maduro on Polymarket.\n\nID: 4155712\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: koat.com\nSLUG: 71476250\nTEXT: George Santos, a former Republican congressman, has been under investigation by the Department of Justice after Kalshi, an online prediction marketplace, reported suspicious trades made by him ahead of President Donald Trump\'s State of the Union address. Santos had boasted about attending the event, then bet against his own attendance, according to a person familiar with the investigation. Kalshi referred Santos to federal prosecutors after detecting the suspicious trades, which have drawn scrutiny from lawmakers who are urging the platforms to do more to guard against insider trading.\n\nID: 4155750\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: khou.com\nSLUG: 507-d15e9792-9eed-41ab-ade3-bf81f1e91241\nTEXT: Rep. George Santos has been reported to federal prosecutors after making suspicious trades on the online prediction marketplace Kalshi ahead of President Donald Trump\'s State of the Union address. Santos boasted about attending the event, then bet against his own attendance, raising red flags with Kalshi. The suspicious trades were detected by a person familiar with the investigation, who spoke to The Associated Press on condition of anonymity.\n\n\n',)
