 a metadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4155717\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: koat.com\nSLUG: 71470669\nTEXT: Iran has halted talks with Israel, amid rising tensions in the region. According to reports by Fars and Tasnim news agencies, Iran had not communicated with Israel on Tuesday after stating that a ceasefire was necessary for negotiations to continue. In other developments, the US military fired a missile to halt an oil tanker trying to reach an Iranian port in violation of the American blockade. The seventh ship stopped by the military, the Botswana-flagged merchant vessel M/T Lexie, ignored repeated warnings over 24 hours before being stopped. US President Donald Trump disputed the claim of halted talks, stating that conversations between him and Israel have been "going on continuously".\n\nID: 4155661\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: khou.com\nSLUG: 507-dab76d64-5533-41db-b68e-48e6355cbcc1\nTEXT: Iran\'s involvement in Lebanon ceasefire talks has stalled after a regional official revealed that Iran had not communicated on Tuesday. The U.S. military fired a missile to halt an oil tanker attempting to reach an Iranian port, the seventh ship stopped by the military since the blockade was enforced. The Botswana-flagged M/T Lexie was stopped after ignoring repeated warnings over 24 hours, with the U.S. Central Command firing a Hellfire missile into its engine room.\n\n\n',)
