 a metadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4155758\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: khou.com\nSLUG: 507-4c2cbd49-9c0a-408e-955b-eda6cbedd2b6\nTEXT: Former President Donald Trump has signed an executive order aimed at improving national security through the use of artificial intelligence (AI). The order, which was characterized as voluntary by the White House, has raised concerns about the vagueness of how the government will decide which AI models qualify for scrutiny and which "trusted partners" will get early access to them. Anthropic, a company that recently announced its most advanced AI model, Claude Mythos, has limited access to the technology and is expanding its group of trusted partners. The company views Trump\'s new order as an important step in strengthening America\'s leadership in AI and is looking forward to collaborating with the White House on its implementation.\n\nID: 4156479\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: cfr.org\nSLUG: assessing-trumps-executive-order-on-ai-oversight\nTEXT: The US government has issued an executive order titled "Promoting Advanced Artificial Intelligence Innovation and Security" to promote AI innovation and security. The order aims to protect American ingenuity and intellectual property from exploitation by adversaries, while also cultivating the country\'s advanced AI-enabled capabilities. The order requests that AI companies voluntarily provide access to "covered frontier models" for a cybersecurity review up to 30 days before their planned release. This move comes as concerns have mounted over the ability of powerful AI models, such as Anthropic\'s Claude Mythos, to autonomously identify and exploit hidden vulnerabilities in real-world software.\n\nID: 4155644\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: ibtimes.sg\nSLUG: trump-signs-sweeping-ai-safety-order-seeks-early-access-advanced-models-ahead-launch-87330\nTEXT: US President signs sweeping AI safety order, allowing early access to advanced models ahead of launch. The directive aims to strengthen cybersecurity defenses by leveraging AI tools, with federal agencies prioritizing the defense of critical infrastructure and government systems within 30 days. A classified benchmarking process will be established to evaluate the cyber capabilities of advanced AI systems, with voluntary pre-release access for companies to engage with the government and provide access to their models for up to 30 days. The administration seeks to encourage secure innovation by allowing experts and trusted partners to assess advanced systems before wider deployment.\n\nID: 4155822\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: hurriyetdailynews.com\nSLUG: trump-signs-ai-order-giving-government-access-to-powerful-models-222829\nTEXT: US President Trump signed an executive order giving the government access to powerful AI models, contradicting warnings from former AI and crypto czar David Sacks. Sacks had expressed concerns that the measure would slow innovation and harm the US in its AI race with China. The order instructs key government agencies to form an "AI cybersecurity clearinghouse" in collaboration with industry and critical infrastructure operators.\n\n\n',)
